<title>USA: U.S. crop production Sept 11 highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop production Sept 11 highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA Wednesday raised its 1996 corn crop estimate to 8.804 billion bushels and lowered its soybean crop estimate to 2.270 billion bushels.</p>
<p>A month ago, USDA estimated the corn crop at 8.695 billion bushels and the soybean crop at 2.300 billion bushels.</p>
<p>Last year, the corn crop was 7.374 billion bushels and soybean production was 2.152 billion bushels.</p>
<p>USDA said corn yield prospects increased in Illinois, Iowa and Nebraska, but yields decreased in Ohio and Winsconsin.</p>
<p>Overall corn yileds were seen at 120.2 bushels per acre, compared with 118.7 estimated a month ago.</p>
<p>Soybean crop maturity continued to be behind normal, USDA said. Yield was forecast at 35.8 bushels per acre, compared with 36.2 a month ago.</p>
<p>High temperatures in California and dry conditions in Louisiana and Arkansas cut USDA's cotton production estimate to 17.900 million bales from 18.577 million a month ago.</p>
<p>Analyst estimates for corn production averaged 8.857 bill ion bushels and for soybeans 2.240 billion.</p>
